# Architecture & conventions

## Request flow

`MicButton` / demo button → `app/page.tsx` POST `{ prompt }` to `/api/build` → `lib/cursor.ts` `runBuild()` → frames streamed back → `handleEvent()` in `page.tsx` updates UI.

Do **not** switch to GET + `EventSource`; the prompt travels in the POST body.

## SSE contract

`/api/build/route.ts` emits newline-delimited frames:

```
data: {"type":"status","phase":"building",...}\n\n
```

`lib/events.ts` defines the `BuildEvent` discriminated union — **source of truth**. New event types: add the type there, map in `lib/cursor.ts`, handle in `page.tsx` `handleEvent`, render in the relevant component.

`lib/events.ts` must stay free of server-only imports (imported by client and server).

## Agent routes

Both `/api/build` and `/api/proof` require:

```ts
export const runtime = "nodejs";
export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";
```

`@cursor/sdk` is in `serverExternalPackages` (`next.config.ts`) — do not import it from client components.

## One agent per request

SDK allows one active run per agent (`409 agent_busy`). Each build: `Agent.create` → `send` → stream → `wait` → `agent[Symbol.asyncDispose]()`. Do not resume agents or fire concurrent runs. `page.tsx` `runningRef` blocks overlapping client requests.

## Scratch workspace & proof

Agent scaffolds into `{os.tmpdir()}/say-so/workspace/` (`WORKSPACE_DIR` in `lib/scratch.ts`), **outside the repo** so Next dev watcher does not reload mid-build.

Before each run, `resetScratch()` wipes workspace and rewrites `proof/screenshot.mjs`.

Win condition path:
1. `lib/prompts.ts` instructs agent to run `node PROOF_SCRIPT WORKSPACE_DIR PROOF_PATH`
2. Agent writes `{tmpdir}/say-so/proof/proof.png`
3. `lib/cursor.ts` checks `proofExists()`, yields `{ type: "proof", url: "/api/proof?t=..." }`
4. `/api/proof` reads that file from disk (`readProof()`), returns `image/png`, `Cache-Control: no-store`

Do not rely on undocumented SDK artifact fields; proof is a steered file on disk.

## Prompts

Agent instructions live in `lib/prompts.ts` `buildPrompt()`. Keep prescriptive: exactly three files (`index.html`, `styles.css`, `app.js`), vanilla JS, no npm/build/network, one screenshot command. Demo reliability depends on this staying tight.
